<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 25 February, from 138 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">138 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,888 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hadrian adopts Antoninus Pius as his heir</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hadrian made Antoninus his successor on condition that he adopt Marcus Aurelius and Lucius Verus. The arrangement secured more than four decades of stable rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1570 CE <span class="tih-ago">456 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Pius V excommunicates Elizabeth I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Regnans in Excelsis declared Elizabeth a heretic and released her subjects from obedience. English Catholics came to be seen as potential traitors, and persecution intensified.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1836 CE <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Colt patents his revolver</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colt received a US patent for a revolving-cylinder pistol. His first company failed, but orders during the Mexican-American War made Colt revolvers famous worldwide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1870 CE <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hiram Revels becomes the first African American US Senator</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mississippi minister was sworn in after a fierce debate over his eligibility. He filled the seat Jefferson Davis had left when the South seceded.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1932 CE <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Adolf Hitler acquires German citizenship</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stateless since renouncing his Austrian citizenship in 1925, Hitler was given a nominal post in the state of Brunswick, making him a German citizen. He could now stand for President.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philippines" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippines.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1986 CE <span class="tih-ago">40 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">People Power Revolution forces Marcos from the Philippines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After days of peaceful mass protest, Ferdinand Marcos fled Manila for Hawaii and Corazon Aquino was sworn in as president. His two decades of rule had included years of martial law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li></ol>
